(841133, 92741, 20235, '<td valign="top">Doh! Another ribbon eludes me :P<br/> <br/>Thanks for the kind comments and feedback everyone. I had alot of fun shooting this photo. Glad to see it did so well.</td>', 'Doh! Another ribbon eludes me :P Thanks for the kind comments and feedback everyone. I had alot of fun shooting this photo. Glad to see it did so well.', '2004-08-04 02:37:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(841146, 93511, 19871, '<td valign="top">If I had been able to do more editing on the photo there is a couple of things I would have done....<br/> <br/>I''d probably have de-saturated (or at least toned down) the whole photo, with a second layer that retained the original colours then erased the semi-de-saturated layer to reveal the eyes.<br/> <br/>On the photo, i definatly overdid the selective de-saturation as IMO the face looks to "grey," perhaps if she had worn blue/purple lipstick the impact would have been better.<br/> <br/>I was quite supprised at the number of low scores I recieved.... shame the reasons wernt given apart from the people that commented both good and bad... after all without the comments how can one gather the reasons?<br/> <br/>I do know I was bumped down for "not meeting the challenge," but for me I took object to mean any physical object (and not the conitation that a woman is an object) and as I see the woman in question just about every day... it [the photo] fulfills the everyday criteria part.<br/> <br/>I have to also say.. the guy that did the toilet paper on the lass... that one should have done very much better as it was a cracking take on the challenge and was definatly thinking out of the box. While It didnt do as well as I feel it should have, it was the kind of lateral thinking that would probably make a fortune in the advertising industry.<br/> <br/></td>', 'If I had been able to do more editing on the photo there is a couple of things I would have done.... I''d probably have de-saturated (or at least toned down) the whole photo, with a second layer that retained the original colours then erased the semi-de-saturated layer to reveal the eyes. On the photo, i definatly overdid the selective de-saturation as IMO the face looks to "grey," perhaps if she had worn blue/purple lipstick the impact would have been better. I was quite supprised at the number of low scores I recieved.... shame the reasons wernt given apart from the people that commented both good and bad... after all without the comments how can one gather the reasons? I do know I was bumped down for "not meeting the challenge," but for me I took object to mean any physical object (and not the conitation that a woman is an object) and as I see the woman in question just about every day... it [the photo] fulfills the everyday criteria part. I have to also say.. the guy that did the toilet paper on the lass... that one should have done very much better as it was a cracking take on the challenge and was definatly thinking out of the box. While It didnt do as well as I feel it should have, it was the kind of lateral thinking that would probably make a fortune in the advertising industry. ', '2004-08-04 02:43:58.000000', NULL, 0),
