(841167, 93206, 2612, '<td valign="top">Great shot! The lighting and composition create a very unique and detailed view of the textures in the glass. The use of yellow and blue is also excellent. I gave it a seven, but it might have slid up the scale another notch if I had completed my second pass at voting.</td>', 'Great shot! The lighting and composition create a very unique and detailed view of the textures in the glass. The use of yellow and blue is also excellent. I gave it a seven, but it might have slid up the scale another notch if I had completed my second pass at voting.', '2004-08-04 02:52:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(841168, 93860, 24486, '<td valign="top">This is my first attempt at dpchallenge and I just want to say a big thank you to all of those who took the time to view and vote on this photograph.<br/> <br/>The original "island" was a coffee table in my lounge and the concept to use a rock came from a visit to the beach.Unfortunetly when I returned to the beach the following day, the tide was on the way out and the rock that had been chosen was now nowhere near the water.Even in this shot there is only just a trickle of water in front of the rock that was used so the effect was lost.My timing of the sun wasnt to wonderful either.The sun was high in a cloudless sky and even playing around with the exposure levels didnt quite help me to pull it off.<br/> <br/>In case you are wondering, the remotes are none the worse for their big day out at the beach.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-01-05 20:12:13.</i></td>', 'This is my first attempt at dpchallenge and I just want to say a big thank you to all of those who took the time to view and vote on this photograph. The original "island" was a coffee table in my lounge and the concept to use a rock came from a visit to the beach.Unfortunetly when I returned to the beach the following day, the tide was on the way out and the rock that had been chosen was now nowhere near the water.Even in this shot there is only just a trickle of water in front of the rock that was used so the effect was lost.My timing of the sun wasnt to wonderful either.The sun was high in a cloudless sky and even playing around with the exposure levels didnt quite help me to pull it off. In case you are wondering, the remotes are none the worse for their big day out at the beach.', '2004-08-04 02:52:42.000000', '2010-01-05 20:12:13.000000', 0),
