(841346, 94118, 3649, '<td valign="top">*shrug*<br/>I expected about as much. I personally love the photo, but prefer a slightly better post-processed version I did when I wasn''t rushing to get this entered :)  <a href="//www.noestudios.com/photo/fm/theKnife_flat.jpg" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">The Reworked Version</a> <br/> <br/>"underexposed" and "lighting from other than dead on" don''t get the point of this, which is understandable. This is, in fact, a brand new knife. I styled it with an ace bandage, electrical tape, band-aids and a mixture of hoisin sauce and cocoa powder.<br/> <br/>The lighting is provided via my makeshift ring flash wannabe - a magnifying work light with a circline fluorescent tube (magnifier removed) about 12" from the subject at 16mm.<br/> <br/>Original inspiring work by David Emmite.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-08-04 03:10:08.</i></td>', '*shrug*I expected about as much. I personally love the photo, but prefer a slightly better post-processed version I did when I wasn''t rushing to get this entered :)  The Reworked Version  "underexposed" and "lighting from other than dead on" don''t get the point of this, which is understandable. This is, in fact, a brand new knife. I styled it with an ace bandage, electrical tape, band-aids and a mixture of hoisin sauce and cocoa powder. The lighting is provided via my makeshift ring flash wannabe - a magnifying work light with a circline fluorescent tube (magnifier removed) about 12" from the subject at 16mm. Original inspiring work by David Emmite.', '2004-08-04 04:09:02.000000', '2004-08-04 04:10:08.000000', 0),
