(842211, 94106, 10686, '<td valign="top">Ummm the frame, and the guy''s body are OK. The lighting is not so good, it really doesn''t add anything to the shot. The expression is terrible. I''m not sure what his face is supposed to say, but it looks like he just projectile vomited at the viewer. That was my first thought when I saw it. Not appealing.</td>', 'Ummm the frame, and the guy''s body are OK. The lighting is not so good, it really doesn''t add anything to the shot. The expression is terrible. I''m not sure what his face is supposed to say, but it looks like he just projectile vomited at the viewer. That was my first thought when I saw it. Not appealing.', '2004-08-04 13:35:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(842318, 93330, 772, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club :)<br/> <br/>Hi Train...<br/> <br/>This is a good example of everyday objects.  Blue jeans are quite commonplace and most people are familiar with them.  The texture and detail here are also somewhat interesting, but the point of focus seems a bit off.  The fasteners/snaps here probably should be in nice sharp focus.  In an image like this one, I can''t see any particular reason for everything not to be sharp.  Compositionally, there is an ajustment you could have made that would possibly create more visual appeal.  The label that is showing in the back of the pants is not really adding anything to the image, but the break in the curve on the bottom left is a bit uncomfortable.  Changing the camera angle slightly would have included this entire curve and probably removed the label.  The additional ''flow'' in the image with that curve being complete would be nice :)<br/> <br/>John Setzler<br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club :) Hi Train... This is a good example of everyday objects.  Blue jeans are quite commonplace and most people are familiar with them.  The texture and detail here are also somewhat interesting, but the point of focus seems a bit off.  The fasteners/snaps here probably should be in nice sharp focus.  In an image like this one, I can''t see any particular reason for everything not to be sharp.  Compositionally, there is an ajustment you could have made that would possibly create more visual appeal.  The label that is showing in the back of the pants is not really adding anything to the image, but the break in the curve on the bottom left is a bit uncomfortable.  Changing the camera angle slightly would have included this entire curve and probably removed the label.  The additional ''flow'' in the image with that curve being complete would be nice :) John Setzler', '2004-08-04 14:36:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(842385, 93984, 23561, '<td valign="top">I gave you a 7 on the picture. I was a very clear shot, not blurry at all and the black and white appears to be a good choice. The reasons I didn''t score it higher was because 1)I don''t see a broken parking meter, or even a working parking meter every day and 2) Although it is a good shot the picture has a depressing quaility. Just my thoughts. Good luck on the next challenge.</td>', 'I gave you a 7 on the picture. I was a very clear shot, not blurry at all and the black and white appears to be a good choice. The reasons I didn''t score it higher was because 1)I don''t see a broken parking meter, or even a working parking meter every day and 2) Although it is a good shot the picture has a depressing quaility. Just my thoughts. Good luck on the next challenge.', '2004-08-04 15:02:58.000000', NULL, 0),
