(991200, 94106, 1827, '<td valign="top">Personally, I like the expression.  To me it is the mock expression you make at someone who''s staring at you mouth agape.  To me it seems to say (coupled with the belly) "What are YOU staring at?"  I agree that the lighting is to harsh.  I think the background would work if he''d cropped right at the frame rather than letting you see some behind him.  Not the best photograph in the world, but not deserving of a 1, IMO.</td>', 'Personally, I like the expression.  To me it is the mock expression you make at someone who''s staring at you mouth agape.  To me it seems to say (coupled with the belly) "What are YOU staring at?"  I agree that the lighting is to harsh.  I think the background would work if he''d cropped right at the frame rather than letting you see some behind him.  Not the best photograph in the world, but not deserving of a 1, IMO.', '2004-11-04 09:48:52.000000', NULL, 0),
